WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.793
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:15.518
Unit fifteen: Music & Movies. Today you will give opinions and recommend songs and films.

4
00:00:15.818 --> 00:00:18.378
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:22.427
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.145
Genre.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.461
Genre means a type of music, film or book.

8
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.595
My favorite genre is science fiction.

9
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:34.603
Your turn. Say: Genre.

10
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:38.328
Genre.

11
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.073
Soundtrack.

12
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:43.257
Soundtrack means the music in a film.

13
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.524
The soundtrack was beautiful.

14
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:48.862
Your turn. Say: Soundtrack.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.829
Soundtrack.

16
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:54.259
Plot.

17
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.830
Plot means the story of a film or book.

18
00:00:58.417 --> 00:01:00.463
The plot was full of surprises.

19
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.621
Your turn. Say: Plot.

20
00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.212
Plot.

21
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:08.974
Character.

22
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.111
Character means a person in a story.

23
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:14.832
The main character is a brave girl.

24
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:18.568
Your turn. Say: Character.

25
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:22.504
Character.

26
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.263
Blockbuster.

27
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.202
Blockbuster means a very popular, successful film.

28
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:30.874
That blockbuster made a lot of money.

29
00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:34.147
Your turn. Say: Blockbuster.

30
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.175
Blockbuster.

31
00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:39.895
Streaming.

32
00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:44.357
Streaming means watching or listening online without downloading.

33
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.938
I watch films on a streaming app.

34
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.982
Your turn. Say: Streaming.

35
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:53.985
Streaming.

36
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.751
Lyrics.

37
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.808
Lyrics means the words of a song.

38
00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.138
I know all the lyrics!

39
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.112
Your turn. Say: Lyrics.

40
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:08.084
Lyrics.

41
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:09.793
Melody.

42
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:13.329
Melody means the main tune of a song.

43
00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:15.823
The melody is easy to remember.

44
00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:19.139
Your turn. Say: Melody.

45
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.094
Melody.

46
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:24.979
Fanbase.

47
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:28.854
Fanbase means all the fans of a singer or show.

48
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.589
That band has a huge fanbase.

49
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:34.987
Your turn. Say: Fanbase.

50
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:38.962
Fanbase.

51
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:40.625
Trailer.

52
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:44.650
Trailer means a short video that advertises a film.

53
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.901
Did you see the new trailer?

54
00:02:47.517 --> 00:02:49.670
Your turn. Say: Trailer.

55
00:02:52.533 --> 00:02:53.233
Trailer.

56
00:02:53.983 --> 00:02:54.938
Sequel.

57
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.169
Sequel means a film or book that continues the story.

58
00:02:59.783 --> 00:03:01.702
The sequel comes out next year.

59
00:03:02.317 --> 00:03:04.539
Your turn. Say: Sequel.

60
00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.320
Sequel.

61
00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:10.131
Recommend.

62
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:14.335
Recommend means to say something is good and others should try it.

63
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.415
I recommend this song.

64
00:03:17.017 --> 00:03:19.414
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

65
00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.337
Recommend.

66
00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:27.773
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:31.162
Visal, did you watch the new blockbuster?

68
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.902
Yes! I think the plot is great.

69
00:03:36.017 --> 00:03:37.587
What about the soundtrack?

70
00:03:38.683 --> 00:03:43.263
In my opinion, the soundtrack is amazing. The melody is beautiful.

71
00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.653
Would you recommend it?

72
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.064
Definitely! I think the sequel will be even better.

73
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.724
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:56.338
Grammar focus: Giving opinions.

75
00:03:56.638 --> 00:03:57.778
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:58.483 --> 00:04:00.030
I think the plot is great.

77
00:04:00.917 --> 00:04:03.369
In my opinion, the soundtrack is amazing.

78
00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:06.736
I'd recommend it because the characters are funny.

79
00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.397
Give a reason after your opinion. It makes your opinion stronger.

80
00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.580
Be careful! Don't say: I am agree with you.

81
00:04:17.533 --> 00:04:19.103
Say: I agree with you.

82
00:04:19.403 --> 00:04:22.358
'Agree' is a verb. Don't use 'am' before it.

83
00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.633
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:27.690
My Movie Review.

85
00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.742
Last weekend, I watched a new animated film on a streaming app.

86
00:04:32.733 --> 00:04:35.708
I think the plot is exciting, and the characters are funny.

87
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.501
In my opinion, the soundtrack is the best part.

88
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.787
The melody of the main song is beautiful, and the lyrics are meaningful.

89
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.984
I'd recommend it to everyone, and I can't wait for the sequel.

90
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.044
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:54.883 --> 00:04:57.417
blank my opinion, the film is boring.

92
00:04:57.717 --> 00:05:00.674
A, In. B, On. C, At.

93
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:05.850
The answer is A: In.

94
00:05:06.983 --> 00:05:08.751
The words of a song are the blank.

95
00:05:09.051 --> 00:05:12.716
A, lyrics. B, melody. C, genre.

96
00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.150
The answer is A: lyrics.

97
00:05:19.317 --> 00:05:22.117
A film that continues the story is a blank.

98
00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:25.780
A, sequel. B, trailer. C, plot.

99
00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:31.704
The answer is A: sequel.

100
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.889
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.736
Recommend a movie or song and explain why you like it.

102
00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.074
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:50.374 --> 00:05:58.227
I'd recommend the song 'Count on Me'. In my opinion, the melody is happy, and I think the lyrics teach us about friendship.

104
00:05:58.527 --> 00:06:00.236
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.625
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and giving opinions.

106
00:06:05.925 --> 00:06:11.608
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

107
00:06:11.908 --> 00:06:14.444
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:14.744 --> 00:06:17.733
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

